   the XT60 (30 A, 120 C)                                         23.93 A                                                    [0.80]  printed
   the dock contacts (4 x 9 A at a 10 C rise)                     5.98 A a pin at an even split                              [0.66]  printed; the split NOT HELD (needs the lowest pin at 0.553 of the highest)
   the 25 A blades (MINI 297)                                     95.7 % of rating                                           [0.87]  printed hold at 110 % for 100 h at 25 C; the rerating at 76.25 C NOT HELD
   F2's element (30 A)                                            79.8 % of rating                                           [0.80]  printed hold; its own range is the battery stream's
   the pack path's copper (2 oz family, 19.57 mm a face)          9.16 K steady                                              [0.92]  decision 35's model (record section 14)
   the barrel field (16 of 0.4 mm)                                0.75 A a barrel, 7.62 K                                    [0.76]  decision 35's model
   the Keystone 3568 holder                                       no current rating printed                                  [-]  DESIGN DEFECT DD-4 (NOT HELD)
   the parts' fractions are of the printed rating, the pair's of its 150 C rise, the breaker FETs' of TI's 125 C rise, the copper's of 10 K

5. THE PROTECTION TABLE (case | current, duration | largest actual trip threshold | longest clearing time | limiting component | margin | evidence)
   10 A continuous | 10.0 A held | none reached (18.32 A least) | not a fault | the XT60, 0.33 of 30 A | 0.67 | printed
   18 A for 60 s | 18.0 A, 60 s | none reached (18.32 A least; 21.08 A typical, +17 %) | not a fault; firmware ends it | Q39/Q40, TJ 133.0 C (33.12 K/W, from 76.25 C) | 17.0 K | derived (E11-29 a target)
   an overload under the unit's limit, held | 18.00 to 23.93 A, indefinitely | 23.93 A largest (VCL 61.5 mV, RS -1.5 %) | none: held by design | Q39/Q40, TJ 176.5 C at 33.12 K/W | OVER 26.5 K; 0 at 24.37 K/W | DESIGN DEFECT DD-2 (L4-E11)
   an overload over the unit's limit | limited to 23.93 A at most, then off | 23.93 A largest | 1.29 ms from the onset (timer 0.897, gate 0.395); regulated after tCL (45 us typ., no max.) | the breaker FET, 40.3 W for 1.29 ms vs 71.1 W | 0.57 (TI <= 0.67) | derived: power limit's spread at 5 mV not printed
   a hot short, board P's FETs welded | 240 to 480 A prospective | 50.59 A largest (VCB 130 mV) | 16.5 us to the release, then as the row above: 1.31 ms | the breaker FET's peak before the gate is low (loop L NOT HELD); IDM 400 A | 0.13 of IDM at the CB (TI's rule); peak not computable | MISSING (E-3, Q-TI-L9S-1)
   a start into a short | 2.40 A at most (PLIM/VIN) | the power limit | 1.29 ms | the breaker FET, as an overload | 0.57 | derived
   a start (gauge FET on, retry, assembly) | 0.659 A at most for 40.7 ms | none: 11.1 W < 24.7 W least | not a fault | the breaker FET, 11.1 W for 20.3 ms vs 19.0 W (DC line) | 0.58 (TI <= 0.67) | derived; IF-1 (loads off)
   docking a live pack | E11-30's 242.9 A peak, cut by the breaker | 50.59 A largest | 16.5 us to the release; the 2.10 ms charge outlasts the timer: off, 0.22 s dwell, then a start | the breaker FET: 242.9 A vs IDM 400 A; 244.1 A at 10 us at 16.8 V | 0.61 of IDM; 0.99 of the 10 us line | derived; MISSING (E-3)
   a persistent fault, retrying | the power limit at 1.33 % duty at most (0.5 % typ.) | as above | each try as above | the breaker FET, 0.53 W average, case 103.0 C | in the derating above | derived
   the shore input, Q7 shorted | F1's envelope (not through board P) | F1, 10 A MINI | section 14.6 | J_DCIN, R19 | OVER | DESIGN DEFECT DD-3 (L4-E11)
   the supported envelope: 10.0 A held and 18.0 A for 60 s from 76.25 C with no trip on any unit; currents to 18.32 A held on every unit;
   between 18.32 and 23.93 A a unit holds or clears by its own threshold; above 23.93 A every unit clears within 1.29 ms of its limit's onset;
   no firmware and no working FET of board P in that path; held currents protect Q39/Q40 only once DD-2 closes

6. DESIGN DEFECTS (unresolved, each with its owner)
   DD-1 W4DP-F2: no firmware-independent element opens the discharge path with board P's FETs welded; the breaker of section 3 is drafted here, not drawn; owner board P's generator with W4DP-F2's owner (the battery stream)
   DD-2 Q39/Q40 pass 150 C held over 21.38 A (+70 C) or 20.53 A (76.25 C) at E11-29's 33.12 K/W; the breaker's largest actual limit 23.93 A asks 24.37 K/W (26.43 K/W from +70 C); owner L4-E11 (E11-29's target), with (L9STK CU)'s copper as the pair's spreader
   DD-3 R19 passes its 3 W and J_DCIN its VH rating inside F1's envelope on the shore input (section 14.6); owner L4-E11
   DD-4 the Keystone 3568 holder prints no current rating; owner Layer 6/7
   INTERFACE DEMANDS
   IF-1 board A's loads on VSYS stay off until the breaker's start ends (at most 40.7 ms after the pack's side rises) or follow its PGD; otherwise the start meets its power limit and retries; owner L4-E11 with board A's generator
   IF-2 each breaker FET on its own pad of at least 1 in2 of 2 oz copper on board P (the sheet's RthJA board); the controller beside RS; VIN's bypass at RS (the sheet's 11.1); owner board P's generator
   IF-3 the energy chain: a stage for the breaker between PACK_FETS and PACK_LEAD (its limit 23.93 A, its rating evidence this record); owner the energy chain's owner (the integrator)
   IF-4 the gauge's OCD1/OCD2 stay the first level with working FETs; a unit whose actual limit is under OCD1's 20 A acts first (1.29 ms); owner the firmware owner (no change asked)
   MISSING PHYSICAL EVIDENCE (specimen; acceptance; supplier task)
   E-1 Q39/Q40's installed path (E11-29 retargeted): the coupon of L4-E11 section 17 with the pack band carrying its current; (Zself + Zmut) at most 24.37 K/W steady from 76.25 C; the supplier measures by the body diode's VSD method
   E-2 the breaker's power limit at its design point: six LM5069-2 on the board P specimen; the regulated current with the output shorted at 16.8 V within 1.47 to 2.40 A, at -40, 25 and 125 C; the supplier's bench, against Q-TI-L9S-1
   E-3 the hot short and the live docking: the board P specimen with Q1/Q2 bypassed, the 12 AWG lead, board E and board A as built, on a charged block; 10 shorts and 100 dockings at a 75 C base: the gate low within 16.5 us of VCB, the peak current and VIN to SENSE recorded, VCL read back within 48.5 to 61.5 mV, each FET's RDS(on) within +5 %; the supplier's fault bench
   E-4 the dock contacts' split: the four-pin set of the fitted lot; the lowest pin resistance at least 0.553 of the highest; each pin at mid-stroke
   E-5 the cells' parallel split: each series group of the built block; no cell over 8 A at 23.93 A (the groups' currents measured); the pack builder
   E-6 R17, R10 and the breaker's sense derated: the makers' sheets; each at its reading in section 4 at the band's temperature; Layer 6 files the sheets
   E-7 the blades' rerating at the inside air: Littelfuse 297's temperature rerating curve; 23.93 A held at 76.25 C; Layer 6 reads the curve
   E-8 Q1/Q2's installed path and their own RDS(on) at temperature: board P's first specimen; the CSD17570Q5B's Figure 8; TJ under 150 C at 23.93 A held from 76.25 C; board P's generator; Layer 6
   MAKER QUESTIONS
   Q-TI-L9S-1 LM5069: the power limit's accuracy at VSNS 5.05 mV (the table prints it at 25 mV); VIN to SENSE above its 0.3 V maximum for the microseconds before the gate is low in a hot short (117 A on this sense) (drafted, not sent)

7. PREDICATES
   no existing element opens below the pair's 150 C current without firmware, with the FETs welded          yes
   a trip allowed at the cells' 24 A leaves Q39/Q40 over 150 C at 22 and 23 A held                          yes
   the sense lies in its window (largest limit at most the cells' current, least above the service)         yes
   the breaker's largest actual limit is at most the cells' continuous current                              yes
   the breaker's least actual limit is above the 18 A service                                               yes
   the typical limit is at least 10 % above the service (SLVA673A)                                          yes
   the power limit's sense voltage is at least the 5 mV floor at the pack's full voltage                    yes
   a start never reaches the power limit or the current limit                                               yes
   the fault pulse is inside the derated SOA with TI's 1.5x margin                                          yes
   the start is inside the derated SOA with TI's 1.5x margin                                                yes
   the breaker FETs hold the largest held current under 125 C                                               yes
   the FET's pulsed rating exceeds the breaker's threshold and the docking peak                             yes
   the gate's 12.6 V is inside the FET's VGS rating                                                         yes
   the clamp stands off the pack, clamps under the FET's VDS and takes the breaker's current                yes
   the controller runs over the pack's range                                                                yes
   the clamp is a part the kit already uses                                                                 yes
   a live docking's power-limited charge outlasts the longest timer (it ends in a retry and a dv/dt start)  yes
   Q39/Q40 need a stronger path than E11-29's target at the breaker's largest limit (DD-2 stands)           yes
   without the power limit the fault pulse would pass the SOA (the limit is relied on)                      yes
